{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UnymkT4TqttJptQyW7pS2g","type":"tool_result","content":"1257 PLAN.md\n1:# Karate Champon\n11:## 0. At a glance\n28:## 1. The source, and what we keep\n30:### 1.1 Research summary (what was confirmed)\n40:### 1.2 Design pillars (source trait → our mechanic)\n51:### 1.3 Narrative tone\n56:## 2. Game overview\n58:### 2.1 Core loop (write this sentence as a comment at the top of the game code)\n61:### 2.2 Modes (main menu)\n71:### 2.3 Story synopsis\n76:## 3. Controls and UX\n78:### 3.1 The twin-stick technique system (the heart of the game)\n99:### 3.2 Device mappings\n115:### 3.3 Prompts and glyphs\n126:### 3.4 10-foot rules (all screens)\n140:### 3.5 Touch-only devices\n147:## 4. Combat system\n149:### 4.1 Fighter body and stage geometry\n157:### 4.2 Technique table (authoritative data; frames are at 60 fps, and the engine steps at 120 Hz, so multiply by 2)\n195:### 4.3 Height and state rules\n203:### 4.4 Block\n209:### 4.5 Scoring a hit\n219:### 4.6 Simultaneous hits (*aiuchi*)\n222:### 4.7 Hit reactions\n227:### 4.8 Facing and cross-ups\n234:## 5. Bout rules and the referee\n236:### 5.1 Terms\n241:### 5.2 Bout state machine (`KC.Bout`, deterministic; all timings × `TUNE.refPace`)\n269:### 5.3 Referee and judges (`KC.Referee`)\n304:### 5.4 Fight HUD (drawn on the canvas in `r.overlay`, anchored to `r.W`/`r.H`)\n316:## 6. CPU AI (`KC.KarateAI`)\n318:### 6.1 Architecture\n335:### 6.2 Personalities\n349:### 6.3 Balance targets (asserted by `ai.test`, §18)\n356:## 7. Content\n358:### 7.1 Roster\n379:### 7.2 Stages (8 fight stages and 3 bonus locations)\n408:### 7.3 Champon Road (the story ladder, `KC.DATA.ladder`)\n435:### 7.4 Bonus stages\n459:### 7.5 Practice (Senpai's drill, `KC.Drill`)\n469:### 7.6 Items and objects\n472:### 7.7 Story beats\n477:## 8. Modes and screens (flow)\n489:### 8.1 Title\n495:### 8.2 Character select (versus)\n501:### 8.3 Champon Road screen\n505:### 8.4 Results (versus)\n508:### 8.5 Stage select\n511:### 8.6 Move List (pause item and DOJO)\n515:### 8.7 Continue, game over and initials\n520:### 8.8 Records\n523:### 8.9 Pause menu\n530:### 8.10 Options (game settings beside the engine's standard ones)\n543:### 8.11 About / Credits\n555:## 9. Art direction and assets\n557:### 9.1 Look\n572:### 9.2 Effects\n580:### 9.3 New art to make (by code)\n615:### 9.4 The bull (custom creature, `KC.Bull`)\n628:### 9.5 Palette and lighting\n633:## 10. Animation\n635:### 10.1 Base system\n638:### 10.2 New karate animations (EC7, or game-side rig post-processing)\n675:## 11. Audio (all generated in code, no files)\n677:### 11.1 Music\n700:### 11.2 Sound effects (`audio.define`)\n708:### 11.3 Gibberish voices (`KC.Voice`, an Animalese/Simlish-style synth on Web Audio)\n727:## 12. Multiplayer: local and AI Hub online\n729:### 12.1 Local\n733:### 12.2 AI Hub session protocol v1 (read `lib/hub/README.md` whole before M10)\n758:### 12.3 Roles\n763:### 12.4 Kachinuki rules online\n770:### 12.5 Messages (JSON, compact; ≤ 16 KB, ≤ 20 per second per copy)\n781:### 12.6 Netcode details\n796:## 13. Attract mode (`KC.Attract`)\n808:## 14. Dev mode (`KC.Dev`)\n848:## 15. Architecture and modules\n850:### 15.1 Folder layout (all dev files inside the dev folder; only the final HTML and `exit-interview.json` sit beside PLAN.md)\n867:### 15.2 Source files (each a fragment of one shared IIFE that starts `const E = My3D2dge`, `'use strict'`; the namespace is `const KC = {}`, exposed as `window.KC` for tests)\n904:### 15.3 Data schemas (designers extend the game by editing these; systems never hard-code content)\n912:### 15.4 Engine changes (keep a record in `engine/CHANGES.md`; rerun `node kits/test.mjs fighting arcade` after each one)\n922:### 15.5 Game configuration\n940:### 15.6 `game.debug` (for tests and the engine's tools)\n951:### 15.7 Build and bundle\n968:## 16. Build order and milestones\n989:## 17. Riskiest parts and how to de-risk them\n1006:## 18. Testing plan\n1008:### 18.1 The one command\n1018:### 18.2 Headless suites (what each checks)\n1083:### 18.3 Browser suites (Playwright, the engine's pinned 1.63.0)\n1096:### 18.4 What only a person can judge (do it by eye, with screenshots and filmstrips)\n1101:## 19. Hand-off checklist (the build's final step)\n1103:### 19.1 Definition of done (from TASK.md)\n1110:### 19.2 About screen, chat reply and exit interview (one source: `data/about.json`)\n1140:### 19.3 Operational rules (from TASK.md; repeated here because they are easy to miss)\n1145:### 19.4 Requirements traceability\n1174:## Appendix A: Text (terse, ALL CAPS; voices are gibberish, these are the subtitles)\n1247:## Appendix B: Default input preset (`KC_KEYS`, single player)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21963457-337f-4dbb-ac8d-3bb95e6cc630","uuid":"68d25a00-ee2c-40bf-b571-66bda0070823","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:38:53.351Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1257 PLAN.md\n1:# Karate Champon\n11:## 0. At a glance\n28:## 1. The source, and what we keep\n30:### 1.1 Research summary (what was confirmed)\n40:### 1.2 Design pillars (source trait → our mechanic)\n51:### 1.3 Narrative tone\n56:## 2. Game overview\n58:### 2.1 Core loop (write this sentence as a comment at the top of the game code)\n61:### 2.2 Modes (main menu)\n71:### 2.3 Story synopsis\n76:## 3. Controls and UX\n78:### 3.1 The twin-stick technique system (the heart of the game)\n99:### 3.2 Device mappings\n115:### 3.3 Prompts and glyphs\n126:### 3.4 10-foot rules (all screens)\n140:### 3.5 Touch-only devices\n147:## 4. Combat system\n149:### 4.1 Fighter body and stage geometry\n157:### 4.2 Technique table (authoritative data; frames are at 60 fps, and the engine steps at 120 Hz, so multiply by 2)\n195:### 4.3 Height and state rules\n203:### 4.4 Block\n209:### 4.5 Scoring a hit\n219:### 4.6 Simultaneous hits (*aiuchi*)\n222:### 4.7 Hit reactions\n227:### 4.8 Facing and cross-ups\n234:## 5. Bout rules and the referee\n236:##