 two joysticks) was impossible.\n- **EC2 Standard-setting defaults** (`Settings` constructor): `new E.Game({ defaults: { glyphs: 'playstation' } })` changes a\n  standard setting's default, and Restore defaults returns to it. The task asks for PlayStation glyphs by default.\n- **EC5 Voice bus** (`Audio._init`, `applyVolume`, `bus()`, a standard `voices` slider in Sound): speech (the gibberish voices)\n  gets its own GainNode and volume under master and mute.\nEOF\nnode kits/test.mjs fighting arcade 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Apply EC5 voice bus, record changes, run kit tests"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1947,"cache_read_input_tokens":164500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1947},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21963457-337f-4dbb-ac8d-3bb95e6cc630","uuid":"921f6dad-8611-47ca-8899-1bde8bd1c989","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:40:23.341Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh32VZyZpxqy9eqQb4eq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EfuDUyyipF7BvgUfip6QgS":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='my-3d2dge.js'; s=open(p).read()\nold=\"      this._musBus = c.createGain(); this._musBus.connect(this._master);\\n      this.applyVolume();\"\nnew=\"      this._musBus = c.createGain(); this._musBus.connect(this._master);\\n      this._voiceBus = c.createGain(); this._voiceBus.connect(this._master);   // (EC5, Karate Champon: a bus for speech, with its own volume)\\n      this.applyVolume();\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"this._musBus.gain.value = this.musicVolume * (this._ducked || this.ducked ? .35 : 1); }\"\nnew=\"this._musBus.gain.value = this.musicVolume * (this._ducked || this.ducked ? .35 : 1); if (this._voiceBus) this._voiceBus.gain.value = this.voiceVolume === undefined ? .8 : this.voiceVolume; }\\n  /** (EC5) a bus's GainNode: 'sfx' | 'music' | 'voice' (null before the first sound) */\\n  bus(name) { this._init(); return name === 'music' ? this._musBus : name === 'voice' ? this._voiceBus : this._sfxBus || null; }\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"  background: { group: 'Sound',\"\nnew=\"  voices: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Voices', type: 'slider', value: .8, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.voiceVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },   // (EC5)\\n  background: { group: 'Sound',\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes for Karate Champon (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff)\n\n- **EC1 Right-stick codes** (`Input.tick`, `FIXED_CODES`, `CODE_LABELS`): `PadRAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` are pressed when the right\n  stick passes .5 on its dominant axis (a 4-way gate) and released below .35. Before, the right stick existed only as\n  `input.padAim` and could not be bound to actions, so a twin-stick \"technique stick\" (Karate Champ's two joysticks) was impossible.\n- **EC2 Standard-setting defaults** (`Settings` constructor): `new E.Game({ defaults: { glyphs: 'playstation' } })` changes a\n  standard setting's default, and Restore defaults returns to it. The task asks for PlayStation glyphs by default.\n- **EC5 Voice bus** (`Audio._init`, `applyVolume`, `bus()`, a standard `voices` slider in Sound): speech (the gibberish voices)\n  gets its own GainNode and volume under master and mute.\nEOF\nnode kits/test.mjs fighting arcade 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Apply EC5 voice bus, record changes, run kit tests"}}}
