{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TB6qSBaDXYBMtUhNEc5as3","type":"tool_result","content":"183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n473:- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking opts.seconds (.4), round opts.at (iris and swirl: a world point { x, y, z }, which each scene's camera places, or [x, y] on the screen; its centre by default). With reduce motion each is a plain fade\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1136:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1139:- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n1140:- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n1141:- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n1142:- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n1143:- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n1144:- `menu.game`: its game\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1146:- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1148:- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1150:- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n1151:- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n1152:- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n1153:- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n1154:- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21963457-337f-4dbb-ac8d-3bb95e6cc630","uuid":"1f796188-1b08-467f-923b-ca60275233fb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:40:29.002Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n473:- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking opts.seconds (.4), round opts.at (iris and swirl: a world point { x, y, z }, which each scene's camera places, or [x, y] on the screen; its centre by default). With reduce motion each is a plain fade\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1136:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1139:- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n1140:- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n1141:- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n1142:- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n1143:- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n1144:- `menu.game`: its game\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1146:- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1148:- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1150:- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n1151:- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n1152:- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n1153:- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n1154:- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2098,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2098,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh333NurmZHgQLFBGE2b\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01LBxCoNDdJDE9X8XzxsRqn4\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":155,\"limit\":200},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1036,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":488145,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1036},\"output_tokens\":16,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\",\"uuid\":\"56d206b1-bc1b-45fb-b5a2-f1a261b0aeb1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:40:24.380Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh3337HP8bBRdh99vD2b\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01LBxCoNDdJDE9X8XzxsRqn4\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":155,\"limit\":200}}}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01LBxCoNDdJDE9X8XzxsRqn4\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"155\\t  src/                    the game: plain scripts (no import/export), loaded in this order (src/manifest.json lists it)\\n156\\t    00-core.js            SN namespace, constants, units, math (vec3, frames), RNG streams, hash, Tune registry, event bus\\n157\\t    01-input.js           SN.INPUT preset, control mapping (input + virtual pad -> ShipControls), double-tap, flick detect\\n158\\t    05-data-teams.js      teams, craft specs, pilots, principals, speed classes\\n159\\t    06-data-weapons.js    weapon definitions and pickup tables\\n160\\t    07-data-tracks.js     the four TrackDefs (§4.3), themes\\n161\\t    08-data-season.js     season tiers, events, Grand Prix, unlock rules\\n162\\t    09-data-story.js      every line of dialogue and announcer callout (§4.5)\\n163\\t    10-data-music.js      the songs and stings (engine tracker format + our extensions)\\n164\\t    11-data-about.js      SN.ABOUT: source info, feedback (feeds the About screen AND exit-interview.json)\\n165\\t    20-track.js           TrackSpline, Track (slices, frames, features, queries, racing line, speed profile)\\n166\\t    25-ship.js            Ship state and the physics step (§3.2)\\n167\\t    27-collide.js         ship-ship collisions\\n168\\t    30-weapons.js         pickups, projectiles, mines, beams, waves, effects on ships, absorb\\n169\\t    35-ai.js              AI pilots (line following, speed control, overtaking, pads, weapons, rubber band)\\n170\\t    40-race.js            Race: lifecycle, laps, sectors, positions, finish, modes' rules, rescue, results\\n171\\t    45-replay.js          input recording, deterministic replay, ghost recording/playback, records\\n172\\t    50-audio.js           synth extensions use, engine hum, SFX catalogue, music director, gibberish voice\\n173\\t    55-glyphs.js          button/key/mouse prompt icons, PlayStation and Xbox sets\\n174\\t    60-render.js          World3D world per track, materials, interpolation, cameras, TV director, split screen\\n175\\t    62-shipkit.js         procedural craft meshes, liveries, animation (flaps, glow, roll), ghosts, explosions\\n176\\t    64-trackmesh.js       track ribbon meshes: surface, walls, neon, pads, tunnels, supports, gantries, overclock skin\\n177\\t    66-scenery.js         theme generators: terrain height/color, buildings, rocks, water, aurora, crowds of props\\n178\\t    68-fx.js              weapon FX, trails, sparks, speed lines, shield flashes, rescue drone, weather\\n179\\t    70-hud.js             race HUD (all modes), split-screen HUD, callouts, name tags, reticles, minimap\\n180\\t    75-ui.js              10-foot widget kit (focus, nav, hover, click, prompts) and every front-end screen\\n181\\t    78-season-ui.js       season hub, briefings (E.Dialog + portraits + voice), GP standings, ending\\n182\\t    80-dev.js             dev mode panel, cheats, sliders, reset, debug overlays\\n183\\t    85-attract.js         idle detection, attract playlist, demo cheats\\n184\\t    90-hub.js             AI Hub session: connect, own card, ghost send/receive, progress/result/time-up/end\\n185\\t    95-main.js            new E.Game, scenes, boot steps, wiring, game.debug\\n186\\t  tests/\\n187\\t    run.mjs               THE one command (§7)\\n188\\t    lib/vm.mjs            loads engine + src/ into a Node vm context (headless game)\\n189\\t    lib/bot.mjs           player bot (drives a human ship through the virtual pad)\\n190\\t    unit/ physics/ race/ weapons/ modes/ flow/ season/ hub/  (Node suites, *.test.mjs)\\n191\\t    browser/*.test.mjs    Playwright suites (bundle loads, renders, screenshots, gamepad stub)\\n192\\t    hub/                  harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (pinned copies) + hub.test.mjs\\n193\\t    out/                  screenshots and reports (git-ignored)\\n194\\t  tools/\\n195\\t    bundle.mjs            builds ../SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728.html\\n196\\t    trackcheck.mjs        track validator (App. C algorithm), prints the §4.3 numbers\\n197\\t    medals.mjs            measures the bot's best times per track/class and writes the medal targets (§4.2)\\n198\\t    exit-interview.mjs    writes ../exit-interview.json from src/11-data-about.js and checks it parses\\n199\\t```\\n200\\t\\n201\\t### 2.3 The page and the bundle\\n202\\t\\n203\\tScript order inside the single HTML file (`tools/bundle.mjs` writes it; everything is inline):\\n204\\t\\n205\\t```html\\n206\\t<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head>\\n207\\t<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n208\\t<script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, byte-identical (the hub's rule: first script, right after meta charset) */</script>\\n209\\t<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\">\\n210\\t<title>Snipeout HD</title>\\n211\\t<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"> <meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n212\\t<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\"> <meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n213\\t<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Finish 3 laps first: fastest time wins\\\">\\n214\\t<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Steer A/D or stick · Thrust W or ✕ · Airbrakes Q/E or L2/R2 · Fire Space or □\\\">\\n215\\t<meta name=\\\"hub:type\\\" content=\\\"Game\\\"> <meta name=\\\"hub:players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n216\\t<style>/* as the handoff template: html/body 100%, #stage, #view under #screen, image-rendering: pixelated */</style>\\n217\\t<script type=\\\"importmap\\\">{ \\\"imports\\\": {\\n218\\t  \\\"three\\\": \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.182.0/build/three.webgpu.min.js\\\",\\n219\\t  \\\"three/webgpu\\\": \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.182.0/build/three.webgpu.min.js\\\",\\n220\\t  \\\"three/tsl\\\": \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.182.0/build/three.tsl.min.js\\\",\\n221\\t  \\\"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\\\": \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat@0.19.3/rapier.mjs\\\" } }</script>\\n222\\t</head><body>\\n223\\t<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\">…the handoff template's static boot splash, title SNIPEOUT HD…</div>\\n224\\t<div id=\\\"stage\\\"><canvas id=\\\"view\\\"></canvas><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas></div>\\n225\\t<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js (classic) */</script>\\n226\\t<script>/* src/*.js in manifest order, concatenated, each prefixed with a  // ==== src/<file> ====  marker (classic) */</script>\\n227\\t<script type=\\\"module\\\" onerror=\\\"window.__sn3dFail='load'\\\">/* engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js (ES module, inline) */</script>\\n228\\t</body></html>\\n229\\t```\\n230\\t\\n231\\t- The game is **classic scripts**. They run first, build the game and call `game.start({ boot })`. The 3D add-on is a\\n232\\t  deferred module, so it finishes later.\\n233\\t- Boot step 1 (`'Waking the 3D engine'`) returns a promise. It polls for `My3D2dge.World3D` every 50 ms, then\\n234\\t  `await E.World3D.init(game)`. If the add-on has not appeared after 30 s, or `__sn3dFail` is set, the step throws\\n235\\t  `Error('The 3D engine could not load (three.js from cdn.jsdelivr.net). Check the connection and reload.')`. The\\n236\\t  engine's boot screen shows that error. Headless (Node), the step returns at once and no renderer is made.\\n237\\t- **Every `src/` file is one IIFE**, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, SN = globalThis.SN; … })();`. It registers what\\n238\\t  it exports on `globalThis.SN`. Top-level `const`/`let` would collide once the files are concatenated into one\\n239\\t  script, and in the vm context.\\n240\\t- **No file may touch `E.THREE`, `E.TSL` or `E.World3D` at top level.** Only call them inside functions that run after\\n241\\t  the boot step. This keeps every file loadable in Node for the tests.\\n242\\t- The dev page (`index.html`) loads the same files separately. Serve it with\\n243\\t  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from the dev folder (note the PID, stop it yourself). Day-to-day checks\\n244\\t  use the bundle, which works from `file://`. The CDN imports work cross-origin, and file:// is a secure context, so\\n245\\t  WebGPU is allowed.\\n246\\t- `tools/bundle.mjs` also checks that the inlined hub client equals `vendor/aihub-session.js` byte for byte, that no\\n247\\t  source contains `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX` or `placeholder`, and that no `<script src=` remains. It prints the file size.\\n248\\t\\n249\\t### 2.4 Units, axes, conventions (bugs hide here: unit-test them first)\\n250\\t\\n251\\t- **Engine units everywhere in the sim:** 16 u = 1 m (World3D's `U`). Speeds are u/s, accelerations u/s². Track data\\n252\\t  is written in **metres** and converted once, at load (`×16`). Displayed speed: `km/h = v[u/s] × 0.225`\\n253\\t  (= 3.6 / 16).\\n254\\t- **Axes (the engine's):** x east, y south, z up. This frame is *left-handed*. World3D converts to three.js with\\n255\\t  `toThree(x, y, z) = (x/16, z/16, y/16)`.\\n256\\t- **Angles:** radians from +x toward +y (0 = east, π/2 = south). World3D's camera yaw uses the same.\\n257\\t- **Frames:** for a forward vector `F` and an up vector `U`, **right `R = cross(U, F)`** with the standard cross-product\\n258\\t  formula. Check: F = (1,0,0) east, U = (0,0,1) gives R = (0,1,0) south, which is the right-hand side when heading\\n259\\t  east. Then `U = cross(F, R)`. Write `SN.frame(F, Uhint)` once and unit-test it on 8 headings.\\n260\\t- **Bank:** a positive bank rolls the right edge down. A right-hand turn (heading angle increasing) gets a positive\\n261\\t  bank. Banked `R' = R·cos b − U·sin b` and `U' = U·cos b + R·sin b`. Unit test: in a right turn the right edge is lower\\n262\\t  (`z` of `C + R'·w` < `z` of `C − R'·w`).\\n263\\t- **Time:** the engine's fixed step, 1/120 s (`update(dt)`). The sim never reads wall-clock time. `game.alpha` is only\\n264\\t  for drawing.\\n265\\t- **Randomness:** the sim uses `SN.rng(stream)` (wrapping `E.rng(seed)`), one stream per purpose:\\n266\\t  `race.rng('pickup')` and `race.rng('ai:' + i)`. **Never `Math.random` in the sim.** Cosmetic code (particles,\\n267\\t  confetti) may use it.\\n268\\t- **Track coordinates:** `s` is arc length along the centre line in u, 0 at the start line, wrapping at `L`. `u` is\\n269\\t  lateral, positive to the right (along `R'`). `h` is height above the surface, along `U'`. A ship's race progress is\\n270\\t  `p = lap·L + s`.\\n271\\t\\n272\\t### 2.5 Modules and their public surfaces\\n273\\t\\n274\\tThe sim layer (Node-safe, deterministic): `00-core, 01-input (mapping only), 05–11 data, 20-track, 25-ship,\\n275\\t27-collide, 30-weapons, 35-ai, 40-race, 45-replay`. The presentation layer (browser only, reads the sim, never writes\\n276\\tto it): `50-audio, 55-glyphs, 60–68 render/fx, 70-hud, 75/78-ui, 80-dev (UI side), 85-attract (director side),\\n277\\t90-hub (network side)`.\\n278\\t\\n279\\tThe sim talks to presentation through **`race.events`**: an array the race clears at the start of each step and fills\\n280\\tduring it. Examples: `{ t: 'pickup', ship, weapon }`, `{ t: 'fire', ship, weapon }`, `{ t: 'hit', ship, by, weapon,\\n281\\tdmg }`, `{ t: 'wall', ship, impact }`, `{ t: 'scrape', ship, k }`, `{ t: 'pad', ship, kind }`, `{ t: 'land', ship,\\n282\\tangle }`, `{ t: 'roll', ship, ok }`, `{ t: 'lap', ship, lap, time }`, `{ t: 'finish', ship, place, time }`,\\n283\\t`{ t: 'elim', ship, by }`, `{ t: 'respawn', ship }`, `{ t: 'rescue', ship }`, `{ t: 'wrongway', ship }`,\\n284\\t`{ t: 'lock', ship, target }`, `{ t: 'zone', n }`, `{ t: 'drill', id, ok }`. Presentation reads the events every\\n285\\tstep for sounds, particles, HUD callouts and rumble. Tests assert on them.\\n286\\t\\n287\\tKey APIs, as a contract the builders keep:\\n288\\t\\n289\\t```js\\n290\\tconst T = SN.Track.build(SN.TRACKS.solenne)     // throws with a clear message if the data is invalid\\n291\\tT.L; T.slices                                    // slice i at s = i*T.ds (ds ≈ 32 u)\\n292\\tT.frameAt(s, out)                                // { C, F, R, U, w (half width), bank, flags } interpolated\\n293\\tT.surface(s, u, out)                             // { P (surface point), N (normal), wallL, wallR, kind: 'deck'|'gap'|'drop', ceil }\\n294\\tT.locate(P, sHint)                               // local Newton search from sHint -> { s, u, h } (never global)\\n295\\tT.query(x, y, zHint)                             // 2D bucket lookup -> nearest slice with surface below zHint (particles, terrain, cameras)\\n296\\tT.line(s) / T.vline(s)                           // AI racing line lateral offset (u) and target speed (u/s) per class\\n297\\tT.features                                       // pads, pit, tunnels, jumps, openEdges, sectors, grid slots, start\\n298\\tconst R = new SN.Race({ track: T, mode, cls, laps, seed, entrants, rules })   // entrants: [{ pilot, team, control: 'human'|'ai'|'ghost', input }]\\n299\\tR.step(dt); R.ships; R.events; R.state; R.results(); R.hash()\\n300\\tSN.Ship.step(ship, controls, dt, race)           // the physics step (§3.2)\\n301\\tSN.AI.controls(ship, race) -> ShipControls       // also used by the player bot, autopilot and attract\\n302\\tSN.Replay.record(race) / SN.Replay.play(data)    // deterministic re-simulation\\n303\\tSN.Tune.T.<key>                                  // live gameplay variables (§3.15), SN.Tune.reset()\\n304\\t```\\n305\\t\\n306\\t`ShipControls = { steer: -1..1, pitch: -1..1 (+ = nose down), thrust: 0|1, brakeL: 0..1, brakeR: 0..1, fire: bool\\n307\\t(held), firePressed, fireReleased, absorb: bool (pressed), shiftL, shiftR: bool (pressed) }`.\\n308\\t\\n309\\t### 2.6 Scenes (engine scenes) and the flow\\n310\\t\\n311\\t```\\n312\\tboot steps ──► title ──(10 s idle)──► attract ──(any input)──► title\\n313\\t                 │ (touch-only: notice + SETTINGS button; attract still runs)\\n314\\t                 ▼ START\\n315\\t               menu ──► setup (class → track → team/pilot → laps) ──► loading ──► race ──► results ──► replay\\n316\\t                 │                                                                  ▲        │\\n317\\t                 ├──► season (tiers, events, briefings, GP standings, ending) ──────┘        └──► menu / retry / next\\n318\\t                 ├──► academy (a race mode) · time trial · hot lap · snipeout · overclock · versus (join P2)\\n319\\t                 └──► how to play · settings (engine) · about/credits\\n320\\tAIHub.active ──► session (own card ─► race ─► round over)   (no title, menus or attract)\\n321\\t```\\n322\\t\\n323\\t- `race` is the only `pausable: true` scene. It is not pausable in a hub session. Its pause menu is the engine's.\\n324\\t  **`menu.items` may be a function**: the engine calls it each time the pause screen opens and drops falsy entries\\n325\\t  (verified in the engine: `v(this._game.o.menu.items)` then `.filter(Boolean)`), so the items can depend on the\\n326\\t  mode. It has: Resume (engine), **Restart**, **Camera** (cycles), **How to play**, **Dev mode**, Settings,\\n327\\t  Controls, Full screen (engine), and Quit (engine, `quit: 'menu'`; `false` in a session). In Overclock and Hot Lap it\\n328\\t  also has **End run**, which counts as finishing.\\n329\\t- Every scene's `draw(r)` calls `world.draw(r)` for the 3D picture first (the active world: the hangar for menus, the\\n330\\t  track for races and the title), then its 2D UI in `r.overlay`.\\n331\\t- `game.debug = { snapshot(), teleport(s, u), … }` (§7) exposes the state for tests and `tools/check.mjs`.\\n332\\t\\n333\\t### 2.7 Engine changes (make them in M0–M2; mark each `// SNIPEOUT EDIT:`)\\n334\\t\\n335\\t1. **Button symbols default to PlayStation, and the option lives in Settings.** In `STANDARD_SETTINGS.glyphs`\\n336\\t   (search `glyphs: { group: 'Controller'`): `group: 'Display'`, `value: 'playstation'`,\\n337\\t   `options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation ✕ ○ □ △'], ['xbox', 'Xbox A B X Y']]`.\\n338\\t2. **Font glyphs ✕ ○ □ △** in both pixel fonts (the `G57` 5×7 table and the `GLYPHS` 3×5 table), so `E.font.text`\\n339\\t   can print `input.label()` results. The pretty colored prompt icons are our own (`55-glyphs.js`). These are the\\n340\\t   fallback inside running text.\\n341\\t3. **Analog buttons.** In `Input.tick`, store `this.padValues[i] = b.value` and add\\n342\\t   `input.value(action) → 0..1`: the largest over its bound codes. Keys and mouse give 1 while held. Pad buttons give\\n343\\t   their `value`. Axis codes give the stick magnitude. Tests can set `input._valueOverride[action]`. Airbrakes use it\\n344\\t   (L2/R2 analog).\\n345\\t4. **Synth extensions in `Audio._voice` / `_note`** (search `_voice(p, bus, t0, mul = 1)`). Oscillator voices accept:\\n346\\t   - `lp: { f, q, env, dec }`: a lowpass BiquadFilter at `f` Hz with resonance `q`, opened by `env` Hz that decays over\\n347\\t     `dec` s (acid bass, plucks);\\n348\\t   - `uni: n, det: cents`: n detuned copies (supersaws);\\n349\\t   - `pan: −1..1`.\\n350\\t\\n351\\t   Music tracks pass them through: `{ wave: 'saw', lp: {…}, uni: 3, det: 12, pan }`. An upper-case note token\\n352\\t   (`'A2!'`) is an accent: louder, and the filter env doubled. Add drum tokens `p` (clap: three 10 ms noise bursts and a\\n353\\t   tail) and `b` (sub boom: sine 55→35 Hz, 0.4 s). Optional sidechain: `duck: .35` on a drums track dips the music bus\\n354\\t   on every `k`.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\",\"uuid\":\"b753308c-bdd0-49f0-b55d-1c86934c191f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:40:24.387Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md\",\"content\":\"  src/                    the game: plain scripts (no import/export), loaded in this order (src/manifest.json lists it)\\n    00-core.js            SN namespace, constants, units, math (vec3, frames), RNG streams, hash, Tune registry, event bus\\n    01-input.js           SN.INPUT preset, control mapping (input + virtual pad -> ShipControls), double-tap, flick detect\\n    05-data-teams.js      teams, craft specs, pilots, principals, speed classes\\n    06-data-weapons.js    weapon definitions and pickup tables\\n    07-data-tracks.js     the four TrackDefs (§4.3), themes\\n    08-data-season.js     season tiers, events, Grand Prix, unlock rules\\n    09-data-story.js      every line of dialogue and announcer callout (§4.5)\\n    10-data-music.js      the songs and stings (engine tracker format + our extensions)\\n    11-data-about.js      SN.ABOUT: source info, feedback (feeds the About screen AND exit-interview.json)\\n    20-track.js           TrackSpline, Track (slices, frames, features, queries, racing line, speed profile)\\n    25-ship.js            Ship state and the physics step (§3.2)\\n    27-collide.js         ship-ship collisions\\n    30-weapons.js         pickups, projectiles, mines, beams, waves, effects on ships, absorb\\n    35-ai.js              AI pilots (line following, speed control, overtaking, pads, weapons, rubber band)\\n    40-race.js            Race: lifecycle, laps, sectors, positions, finish, modes' rules, rescue, results\\n    45-replay.js          input recording, deterministic replay, ghost recording/playback, records\\n    50-audio.js           synth extensions use, engine hum, SFX catalogue, music director, gibberish voice\\n    55-glyphs.js          button/key/mouse prompt icons, PlayStation and Xbox sets\\n    60-render.js          World3D world per track, materials, interpolation, cameras, TV director, split screen\\n    62-shipkit.js         procedural craft meshes, liveries, animation (flaps, glow, roll), ghosts, explosions\\n    64-trackmesh.js       track ribbon meshes: surface, walls, neon, pads, tunnels, supports, gantries, overclock skin\\n    66-scenery.js         theme generators: terrain height/color, buildings, rocks, water, aurora, crowds of props\\n    68-fx.js              weapon FX, trails, sparks, speed lines, shield flashes, rescue drone, weather\\n    70-hud.js             race HUD (all modes), split-screen HUD, callouts, name tags, reticles, minimap\\n    75-ui.js              10-foot widget kit (focus, nav, hover, click, prompts) and every front-end screen\\n    78-season-ui.js       season hub, briefings (E.Dialog + portraits + voice), GP standings, ending\\n    80-dev.js             dev mode panel, cheats, sliders, reset, debug overlays\\n    85-attract.js         idle detection, attract playlist, demo cheats\\n    90-hub.js             AI Hub session: connect, own card, ghost send/receive, progress/result/time-up/end\\n    95-main.js            new E.Game, scenes, boot steps, wiring, game.debug\\n  tests/\\n    run.mjs               THE one command (§7)\\n    lib/vm.mjs            loads engine + src/ into a Node vm context (headless game)\\n    lib/bot.mjs           player bot (drives a human ship through the virtual pad)\\n    unit/ physics/ race/ weapons/ modes/ flow/ season/ hub/  (Node suites, *.test.mjs)\\n    browser/*.test.mjs    Playwright suites (bundle loads, renders, screenshots, gamepad stub)\\n    hub/                  harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (pinned copies) + hub.test.mjs\\n    out/                  screenshots and reports (git-ignored)\\n  tools/\\n    bundle.mjs            builds ../SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728.html\\n    trackcheck.mjs        track validator (App. C algorithm), prints the §4.3 numbers\\n    medals.mjs            measures the bot's best times per track/class and writes the medal targets (§4.2)\\n    exit-interview.mjs    writes ../exit-interview.json from src/11-data-about.js and checks it parses\\n```\\n\\n### 2.3 The page and the bundle\\n\\nScript order inside the single HTML file (`tools/bundle.mjs` writes it; everything is inline):\\n\\n```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, byte-identical (the hub's rule: first script, right after meta charset) */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\">\\n<title>Snipeout HD</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"> <meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\"> <meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Finish 3 laps first: fastest time wins\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Steer A/D or stick · Thrust W or ✕ · Airbrakes Q/E or L2/R2 · Fire Space or □\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:type\\\" content=\\\"Game\\\"> <meta name=\\\"hub:players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<style>/* as the handoff template: html/body 100%, #stage, #view under #screen, image-rendering: pixelated */</style>\\n<script type=\\\"importmap\\\">{ \\\"imports\\\": {\\n  \\\"three\\\": \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.182.0/build/three.webgpu.min.js\\\",\\n  \\\"three/webgpu\\\": \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.182.0/build/three.webgpu.min.js\\\",\\n  \\\"three/tsl\\\": \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.182.0/build/three.tsl.min.js\\\",\\n  \\\"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\\\": \\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat@0.19.3/rapier.mjs\\\" } }</script>\\n</head><body>\\n<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\">…the handoff template's static boot splash, title SNIPEOUT HD…</div>\\n<div id=\\\"stage\\\"><canvas id=\\\"view\\\"></canvas><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas></div>\\n<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js (classic) */</script>\\n<script>/* src/*.js in manifest order, concatenated, each prefixed with a  // ==== src/<file> ====  marker (classic) */</script>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\" onerror=\\\"window.__sn3dFail='load'\\\">/* engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js (ES module, inline) */</script>\\n</body></html>\\n```\\n\\n- The game is **classic scripts**. They run first, build the game and call `game.start({ boot })`. The 3D add-on is a\\n  deferred module, so it finishes later.\\n- Boot step 1 (`'Waking the 3D engine'`) returns a promise. It polls for `My3D2dge.World3D` every 50 ms, then\\n  `await E.World3D.init(game)`. If the add-on has not appeared after 30 s, or `__sn3dFail` is set, the step throws\\n  `Error('The 3D engine could not load (three.js from cdn.jsdelivr.net). Check the connection and reload.')`. The\\n  engine's boot screen shows that error. Headless (Node), the step returns at once and no renderer is made.\\n- **Every `src/` file is one IIFE**, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, SN = globalThis.SN; … })();`. It registers what\\n  it exports on `globalThis.SN`. Top-level `const`/`let` would collide once the files are concatenated into one\\n  script, and in the vm context.\\n- **No file may touch `E.THREE`, `E.TSL` or `E.World3D` at top level.** Only call them inside functions that run after\\n  the boot step. This keeps every file loadable in Node for the tests.\\n- The dev page (`index.html`) loads the same files separately. Serve it with\\n  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from the dev folder (note the PID, stop it yourself). Day-to-day checks\\n  use the bundle, which works from `file://`. The CDN imports work cross-origin, and file:// is a secure context, so\\n  WebGPU is allowed.\\n- `tools/bundle.mjs` also checks that the inlined hub client equals `vendor/aihub-session.js` byte for byte, that no\\n  source contains `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX` or `placeholder`, and that no `<script src=` remains. It prints the file size.\\n\\n### 2.4 Units, axes, conventions (bugs hide here: unit-test them first)\\n\\n- **Engine units everywhere in the sim:** 16 u = 1 m (World3D's `U`). Speeds are u/s, accelerations u/s². Track data\\n  is written in **metres** and converted once, at load (`×16`). Displayed speed: `km/h = v[u/s] × 0.225`\\n  (= 3.6 / 16).\\n- **Axes (the engine's):** x east, y south, z up. This frame is *left-handed*. World3D converts to three.js with\\n  `toThree(x, y, z) = (x/16, z/16, y/16)`.\\n- **Angles:** radians from +x toward +y (0 = east, π/2 = south). World3D's camera yaw uses the same.\\n- **Frames:** for a forward vector `F` and an up vector `U`, **right `R = cross(U, F)`** with the standard cross-product\\n  formula. Check: F = (1,0,0) east, U = (0,0,1) gives R = (0,1,0) south, which is the right-hand side when heading\\n  east. Then `U = cross(F, R)`. Write `SN.frame(F, Uhint)` once and unit-test it on 8 headings.\\n- **Bank:** a positive bank rolls the right edge down. A right-hand turn (heading angle increasing) gets a positive\\n  bank. Banked `R' = R·cos b − U·sin b` and `U' = U·cos b + R·sin b`. Unit test: in a right turn the right edge is lower\\n  (`z` of `C + R'·w` < `z` of `C − R'·w`).\\n- **Time:** the engine's fixed step, 1/120 s (`update(dt)`). The sim never reads wall-clock time. `game.alpha` is only\\n  for drawing.\\n- **Randomness:** the sim uses `SN.rng(stream)` (wrapping `E.rng(seed)`), one stream per purpose:\\n  `race.rng('pickup')` and `race.rng('ai:' + i)`. **Never `Math.random` in the sim.** Cosmetic code (particles,\\n  confetti) may use it.\\n- **Track coordinates:** `s` is arc length along the centre line in u, 0 at the start line, wrapping at `L`. `u` is\\n  lateral, positive to the right (along `R'`). `h` is height above the surface, along `U'`. A ship's race progress is\\n  `p = lap·L + s`.\\n\\n### 2.5 Modules and their public surfaces\\n\\nThe sim layer (Node-safe, deterministic): `00-core, 01-input (mapping only), 05–11 data, 20-track, 25-ship,\\n27-collide, 30-weapons, 35-ai, 40-race, 45-replay`. The presentation layer (browser only, reads the sim, never writes\\nto it): `50-audio, 55-glyphs, 60–68 render/fx, 70-hud, 75/78-ui, 80-dev (UI side), 85-attract (director side),\\n90-hub (network side)`.\\n\\nThe sim talks to presentation through **`race.events`**: an array the race clears at the start of each step and fills\\nduring it. Examples: `{ t: 'pickup', ship, weapon }`, `{ t: 'fire', ship, weapon }`, `{ t: 'hit', ship, by, weapon,\\ndmg }`, `{ t: 'wall', ship, impact }`, `{ t: 'scrape', ship, k }`, `{ t: 'pad', ship, kind }`, `{ t: 'land', ship,\\nangle }`, `{ t: 'roll', ship, ok }`, `{ t: 'lap', ship, lap, time }`, `{ t: 'finish', ship, place, time }`,\\n`{ t: 'elim', ship, by }`, `{ t: 'respawn', ship }`, `{ t: 'rescue', ship }`, `{ t: 'wrongway', ship }`,\\n`{ t: 'lock', ship, target }`, `{ t: 'zone', n }`, `{ t: 'drill', id, ok }`. Presentation reads the events every\\nstep for sounds, particles, HUD callouts and rumble. Tests assert on them.\\n\\nKey APIs, as a contract the builders keep:\\n\\n```js\\nconst T = SN.Track.build(SN.TRACKS.solenne)     // throws with a clear message if the data is invalid\\nT.L; T.slices                                    // slice i at s = i*T.ds (ds ≈ 32 u)\\nT.frameAt(s, out)                                // { C, F, R, U, w (half width), bank, flags } interpolated\\nT.surface(s, u, out)                             // { P (surface point), N (normal), wallL, wallR, kind: 'deck'|'gap'|'drop', ceil }\\nT.locate(P, sHint)                               // local Newton search from sHint -> { s, u, h } (never global)\\nT.query(x, y, zHint)                             // 2D bucket lookup -> nearest slice with surface below zHint (particles, terrain, cameras)\\nT.line(s) / T.vline(s)                           // AI racing line lateral offset (u) and target speed (u/s) per class\\nT.features                                       // pads, pit, tunnels, jumps, openEdges, sectors, grid slots, start\\nconst R = new SN.Race({ track: T, mode, cls, laps, seed, entrants, rules })   // entrants: [{ pilot, team, control: 'human'|'ai'|'ghost', input }]\\nR.step(dt); R.ships; R.events; R.state; R.results(); R.hash()\\nSN.Ship.step(ship, controls, dt, race)           // the physics step (§3.2)\\nSN.AI.controls(ship, race) -> ShipControls       // also used by the player bot, autopilot and attract\\nSN.Replay.record(race) / SN.Replay.play(data)    // deterministic re-simulation\\nSN.Tune.T.<key>                                  // live gameplay variables (§3.15), SN.Tune.reset()\\n```\\n\\n`ShipControls = { steer: -1..1, pitch: -1..1 (+ = nose down), thrust: 0|1, brakeL: 0..1, brakeR: 0..1, fire: bool\\n(held), firePressed, fireReleased, absorb: bool (pressed), shiftL, shiftR: bool (pressed) }`.\\n\\n### 2.6 Scenes (engine scenes) and the flow\\n\\n```\\nboot steps ──► title ──(10 s idle)──► attract ──(any input)──► title\\n                 │ (touch-only: notice + SETTINGS button; attract still runs)\\n                 ▼ START\\n               menu ──► setup (class → track → team/pilot → laps) ──► loading ──► race ──► results ──► replay\\n                 │                                                                  ▲        │\\n                 ├──► season (tiers, events, briefings, GP standings, ending) ──────┘        └──► menu / retry / next\\n                 ├──► academy (a race mode) · time trial · hot lap · snipeout · overclock · versus (join P2)\\n                 └──► how to play · settings (engine) · about/credits\\nAIHub.active ──► session (own card ─► race ─► round over)   (no title, menus or attract)\\n```\\n\\n- `race` is the only `pausable: true` scene. It is not pausable in a hub session. Its pause menu is the engine's.\\n  **`menu.items` may be a function**: the engine calls it each time the pause screen opens and drops falsy entries\\n  (verified in the engine: `v(this._game.o.menu.items)` then `.filter(Boolean)`), so the items can depend on the\\n  mode. It has: Resume (engine), **Restart**, **Camera** (cycles), **How to play**, **Dev mode**, Settings,\\n  Controls, Full screen (engine), and Quit (engine, `quit: 'menu'`; `false` in a session). In Overclock and Hot Lap it\\n  also has **End run**, which counts as finishing.\\n- Every scene's `draw(r)` calls `world.draw(r)` for the 3D picture first (the active world: the hangar for menus, the\\n  track for races and the title), then its 2D UI in `r.overlay`.\\n- `game.debug = { snapshot(), teleport(s, u), … }` (§7) exposes the state for tests and `tools/check.mjs`.\\n\\n### 2.7 Engine changes (make them in M0–M2; mark each `// SNIPEOUT EDIT:`)\\n\\n1. **Button symbols default to PlayStation, and the option lives in Settings.** In `STANDARD_SETTINGS.glyphs`\\n   (search `glyphs: { group: 'Controller'`): `group: 'Display'`, `value: 'playstation'`,\\n   `options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation ✕ ○ □ △'], ['xbox', 'Xbox A B X Y']]`.\\n2. **Font glyphs ✕ ○ □ △** in both pixel fonts (the `G57` 5×7 table and the `GLYPHS` 3×5 table), so `E.font.text`\\n   can print `input.label()` results. The pretty colored prompt icons are our own (`55-glyphs.js`). These are the\\n   fallback inside running text.\\n3. **Analog buttons.** In `Input.tick`, store `this.padValues[i] = b.value` and add\\n   `input.value(action) → 0..1`: the largest over its bound codes. Keys and mouse give 1 while held. Pad buttons give\\n   their `value`. Axis codes give the stick magnitude. Tests can set `input._valueOverride[action]`. Airbrakes use it\\n   (L2/R2 analog).\\n4. **Synth extensions in `Audio._voice` / `_note`** (search `_voice(p, bus, t0, mul = 1)`). Oscillator voices accept:\\n   - `lp: { f, q, env, dec }`: a lowpass BiquadFilter at `f` Hz with resonance `q`, opened by `env` Hz that decays over\\n     `dec` s (acid bass, plucks);\\n   - `uni: n, det: cents`: n detuned copies (supersaws);\\n   - `pan: −1..1`.\\n\\n   Music tracks pass them through: `{ wave: 'saw', lp: {…}, uni: 3, det: 12, pan }`. An upper-case note token\\n   (`'A2!'`) is an accent: louder, and the filter env doubled. Add drum tokens `p` (clap: three 10 ms noise bursts and a\\n   tail) and `b` (sub boom: sine 55→35 Hz, 0.4 s). Optional sidechain: `duck: .35` on a drums track dips the music bus\\n   on every `k`.\",\"numLines\":200,\"startLine\":155,\"totalLines\":2048}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01LBxCoNDdJDE9X8XzxsRqn4\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\",\"uuid\":\"940c155b-b3ea-4803-96cc-a0d139ef1926\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":100,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\",\"uuid\":\"d6b1895d-e240-4d9c-8615-92b888e8345c\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2207,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2207,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":5500,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"b0887348-40c0-4937-a3bc-127909132c3b\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":5600,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"cd38db09-dfc7-48ec-892d-2a3e4c8009cd\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":5700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"f07220c4-8d25-4d95-ae63-eb99b941af3e\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":5850,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"e547b36e-04a1-4597-bb21-54a60dbb6f6c\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2016,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2016,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":90700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"9a1875c9-e5fb-4f0d-9691-2604af5823e7\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":90900,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"3a22f863-2882-475d-8877-3cfe1056024d\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":91100,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"0e26f252-80ee-4ce0-b9f3-805f2e83f05b\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":91300,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"1e7b805b-c28d-4baa-a5ae-f26416bd5f08\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/c