{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LCnVvr5V8CKAqzXT7ADTX2","type":"tool_result","content":"/* =============================================================================\n * 10j. PLAYERS AND SPLIT SCREEN  two to four on one machine. game.players: game.input is player 1 (a game of one is\n *    unchanged), each other an input of its own, with game.input's API, its device and its bindings: a gamepad each, or\n *    half a keyboard each for two (Input.halfKeys: WASD with F G H R T Y on the left, the arrows with . / , L ; ' and the\n *    numpad on the right), touch for player 1. game.allowJoin({ max, onJoin }) lets them in: Start on a free pad, or 2 (the\n *    right half's start) on the keyboard, player 1 then playing on its left half; game.removePlayer(p). Each has player (its\n *    number), name ('P2') and color. A pause says who paused, a lost controller names its player, the Controls screen\n *    has a page each. game.splitScreen(n, { layout, follow }): two to four viewports, each its own camera (viewport.follow,\n *    viewport.focus), the scene drawn once in each (r.viewport says which: { i, x, y, w, h }) and scene.hud(r) once over\n *    the whole screen; GPU lighting off while split. A scene's start ends a split.\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst KEY_HALVES = {   // each half's moves, its buttons in order (the preset's other actions take them in turn) and its menu keys\n  left: { up: ['KeyW'], down: ['KeyS'], left: ['KeyA'], right: ['KeyD'], buttons: [['KeyF'], ['KeyG'], ['KeyH'], ['KeyR'], ['KeyT'], ['KeyY'], ['KeyV'], ['KeyB']], start: ['Digit1'], pause: ['Escape', 'Digit1'], confirm: ['KeyF'], cancel: ['KeyG'] },\n  right: { up: ['ArrowUp'], down: ['ArrowDown'], left: ['ArrowLeft'], right: ['ArrowRight'], buttons: [['Period', 'Numpad1'], ['Slash', 'Numpad2'], ['Comma', 'Numpad3'], ['KeyL', 'Numpad4'], ['Semicolon', 'Numpad5'], ['Quote', 'Numpad6'], ['KeyK',