{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh8Wvn9VkcrRgHn8Dx6s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TUVzqUV5gYZLmahDtxuBzF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183848 && cat > ISSUES.md <<'EOF'\n# Issues found by testing (this build), and their fixes\nGame-breaking (5):\n1. Load crash: Object.assign in the scene helper read the practice scene's `drill` getter at boot (smoke run). Fixed: a plain lookup.\n2. Bout deadlock: fighters who crossed over walked back into each other while push resolution shoved them apart (CPU-vs-CPU stall). Fixed: no pushing while walking to the marks, plus phase timeouts.\n3. Story blocked: the cutscene scene's `done` flag survived from the prologue, so every later cutscene never ended (story playthrough). Fixed: reset on enter (practice's `fin` too).\n4. Story blocked: the reverse-punch drill was impossible (the drill holds you on your mark; the phantom target had no width). Fixed: drills check the stick cell.\n5. Crash: Pots Ahoy! read the reach of a block, which has none (story playthrough). Fixed.\nOthers (20):\n6. Font lacks · — … (drawn as ?). 7. Referee faced away and covered the fight. 8. Stadium scoreboard overlapped the clock.\n9. FULL POINT call used game.after, which never fired when the bout runs alone. 10. Lunge punches reached from the marks (40% of points).\n11. Jumping side kick dominated (always full). 12. CPU reacted too late and blocked into counters. 13. CPU block expired before slow attacks landed.\n14. CPU presses in long recovery overwrote each other. 15. Buffered presses lost their posture. 16. Unlocks lost where storage is blocked (no memory fallback).\n17. Attract aiuchi never synced. 18. Attract's title step was set in draw (skipped headless). 19. Main menu overflowed the screen.\n20. Road NEXT line touched the belt row. 21. Pasture fence drawn over the fighters. 22. About pages mixed text scales and overflowed.\n23. Attract HUD drew 9 point slots. 24. Free-spar dummy label collided with its prompt. 25. Records rows overlapped.\n(Test-tool bugs, not counted: same-URL deep-link screenshots, EC1 needing a fake pad, the Lab's gap search for air moves, python's buffered port line.)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='data/about.json'; a=json.load(open(p))\na['testingFeedback'][0]=\"25 game issues, each listed with its fix in ISSUES.md in the dev folder: scene flags that persisted between visits, a crossed-fighters deadlock, an impossible reverse-punch drill, two crashes, CPU timing bugs, lost buffered presses, lunge and jump-kick imbalance, attract-demo timing, a storage fallback, missing font glyphs, and layout overlaps.\"\na['testingFeedback'][1]=\"5: a crash at load, the walk-back deadlock that froze a bout after fighters crossed, cutscenes that never ended after the first (story blocked), the reverse-punch drill that could not be passed (story blocked), and a Pots Ahoy! crash when the hero blocked.\"\na['testingFeedback'][2]=\"The scripted full playthrough of the Champon Road (story suite): it found three of the five game-breaking bugs, and it drives every scene with real inputs.\"\njson.dump(a,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nEOF\ntimeout 600 node tests/run.mjs --only ui,data 2>&1 | tail -2; node -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8'));console.log(j.testingFeedback[1].slice(0,40))\"","description":"Write the issue log, correct the counts, rebuild and check","timeout":700000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2975,"cache_read_input_tokens":542815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2975},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":n