the belt row. 21. Pasture fence drawn over the fighters. 22. About pages mixed text scales and overflowed.\n23. Attract HUD drew 9 point slots. 24. Free-spar dummy label collided with its prompt. 25. Records rows overlapped.\n(Test-tool bugs, not counted: same-URL deep-link screenshots, EC1 needing a fake pad, the Lab's gap search for air moves, python's buffered port line.)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='data/about.json'; a=json.load(open(p))\na['testingFeedback'][0]=\"25 game issues, each listed with its fix in ISSUES.md in the dev folder: scene flags that persisted between visits, a crossed-fighters deadlock, an impossible reverse-punch drill, two crashes, CPU timing bugs, lost buffered presses, lunge and jump-kick imbalance, attract-demo timing, a storage fallback, missing font glyphs, and layout overlaps.\"\na['testingFeedback'][1]=\"5: a crash at load, the walk-back deadlock that froze a bout after fighters crossed, cutscenes that never ended after the first (story blocked), the reverse-punch drill that could not be passed (story blocked), and a Pots Ahoy! crash when the hero blocked.\"\na['testingFeedback'][2]=\"The scripted full playthrough of the Champon Road (story suite): it found three of the five game-breaking bugs, and it drives every scene with real inputs.\"\njson.dump(a,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nEOF\ntimeout 600 node tests/run.mjs --only ui,data 2>&1 | tail -2; node -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8'));console.log(j.testingFeedback[1].slice(0,40))\"","description":"Write the issue log, correct the counts, rebuild and check","timeout":700000}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TUVzqUV5gYZLmahDtxuBzF","type":"tool_result","content":"KC TESTS: 80 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (0.7 s)\n5: a crash at load, the walk-back deadlo","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21963457-337f-4dbb-ac8d-3bb95e6cc630","uuid":"7b596d2b-895e-4be3-aee9-0470042994e8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:52:45.345Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"KC TESTS: 80 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (0.7 s)\n5: a crash at load, the walk-back deadlo","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183213__xf5fb84/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1966,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1966,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01VodkKYjGJd9XX4ZJYNFckV\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"2026-11-03 19:52:14\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1701386 Nov  3 19:51 ../TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183213.html\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    3211 Nov  3 19:51 ../exit-interview.json\\n  4770 total\\n22\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"14efaf47-c831-41be-b2ba-0398106a097f\",\"uuid\":\"e465cc34-b560-44d8-b44f-fb6051c3adf7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:52:14.522Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"2026-11-03 19:52:14\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1701386 Nov  3 19:51 ../TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183213.html\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    3211 Nov  3 19:51 ../exit-interview.json\\n  4770 total\\n22\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01VodkKYjGJd9XX4ZJYNFckV\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh8X57wojqjhqn9XewUK\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01KmFsRCSFHkjwiWNvpZHa9q\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='src/99-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\\na=\\\"\\\"\\\"  testingFeedback: [],\\n  engineFeedback: [],\\n  promptFeedback: [],\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nb=\\\"\\\"\\\"  testingFeedback: [\\n    'About 25. The headless bot playthroughs and the content validators found most of them: areas that could never be cleared, targets nobody could see or shoot, and crashes. Screenshots found the rest: cover crates filling the stand view, glyphs missing from the font, and HUD overlaps in split screen.',\\n    'Eight were game breaking: grenade and rocket threats that never counted down (you could not take cover from them in time); the Bulldog parked behind a container (1-3 could not be won); canal-bridge and moored-boat enemies the boat left behind (1-4 stuck); a sluice lock hidden behind a catwalk barrier (3-2 stuck); a Training drill stuck on a civilian cut-out; a drone-entry crash; and a load-order crash in the cutscene data.',\\n    'A full ARCADE run by the fair Autopilot bot, headless, logging time, lives and the cause of every hit for each area. It showed exactly which area stalled and why, in seconds.',\\n    'The first smoke test, which only checked for errors after 200 s of play. It passed while the game sat frozen on a continue screen, so it told me nothing until I logged the state of each area.'],\\n  engineFeedback: [\\n    'The Humanoid rigs draw themselves from any View at any scale, so dropping them into my own perspective renderer as depth-tested billboards worked on the first try. E.materialTile and E.shapeMesh exist for exactly this kind of 3D renderer, and the headless game.advance made bot playthroughs of the whole game take seconds.',\\n    'Yes. Timers set with game.after before game.start are cleared by the first scene change; a scene change takes longer than 0.2 s because of the fade, so tests must wait; a crouching Humanoid\\\\\\\\'s head (23.6 u) is taller than crouch-height cover; and input.label returns the PlayStation cross while the pixel font could not draw it.',\\n    'Rail3D, a JavaScript software renderer inside the engine\\\\\\\\'s pixel buffer: perspective-correct textured triangles with near clipping, a z-buffer, the engine\\\\\\\\'s banded light with ordered dither, quantized fog, a procedural sky, depth-tested particles and lines, and engine rigs composited as billboards.',\\n    'The handoff has no 3D engine, so a first-person light-gun game meant building perspective on a 2D engine. Rigs are drawn orthographically with one depth for the whole figure, so hiding behind cover needed care: enemies sink behind low cover and are clipped at the cover\\\\\\\\'s base.',\\n    'Five small patches, logged in engine/PATCHES.md: PlayStation button symbols by default (with Xbox as the option); long guns for Humanoids (rifles with a stock, and gunLen); WheelUp and WheelDown as bindable codes; game.audio.bus() so my Web Audio voice synth and ambience follow the volume settings; and new font glyphs (the cross, circle, square and triangle, plus an em dash, an ellipsis, a middle dot, a gear, infinity and a left arrow).',\\n    'Add a perspective view for rigs and shapes: the same View API with a camera position and field of view, so first-person and rail games can use the engine\\\\\\\\'s own queue, lighting and depth sorting instead of a separate renderer.'],\\n  promptFeedback: [\\n    'The clear contract: exact file names, the four feedback sections in three places, one test command that prints only failures, \\\"TASK.md wins\\\" over the plan, and a detailed plan to start from.',\\n    'The plan\\\\\\\\'s folder and file names (claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174731) differ from the names in TASK.md (medium-20261103-183213), and the plan wants everything inlined while TASK.md allows CDN dependencies. \\\"TASK.md wins\\\" settled both. \\\"Testing: testing parameters allowed\\\" in Source Information was ambiguous.',\\n    'Scope. A three-stage light-gun game with six bosses, a software 3D renderer, AI Hub netcode, split-screen co-op, an attract mode, a dev panel and Training is a lot for one session, and every area had to be winnable and readable, not just present.',\\n    'Say how long the session may run and which plan items may be cut, and give TASK.md\\\\\\\\'s required features as a numbered checklist the final reply can tick off.'],\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\\na=\\\"    usage: 'unknown'\\\"\\nb=\\\"    usage: 'unknown (no token or cost counter was available to me); session time about 1 h 25 min (18:32 to about 19:57)'\\\"\\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\\na=\\\"    research: 'The handoff\\\\\\\\'s engine docs (README, API card, guide, index), the AI Hub protocol README, the plan\\\\\\\\'s Wikipedia-sourced notes on Time Crisis 3 (no new web research)',\\\"\\nb=\\\"    research: 'The handoff\\\\\\\\'s engine docs (README, API card, guide, index) and engine source where needed, the AI Hub protocol README and harness, and the plan\\\\\\\\'s notes on Time Crisis 3 (taken from Wikipedia at planning time); no new web research',\\\"\\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -1; node -e \\\"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8')); console.log(Object.keys(j), j.testingFeedback.length, j.engineFeedback.length, j.promptFeedback.length)\\\"; node tests/run.mjs 2>&1 | tail -3\",\"description\":\"Fill feedback, rebuild, verify exit interview and tests\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2182,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":687012,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2182},\"o